<title>POLAND: Polish grain prices all rise last week.</title>
<headline>Polish grain prices all rise last week.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish wheat, rye and barley prices continued to rise at last week's grain auctions, the Agriculture Ministry said in a statement on Monday.</p>
<p>POLISH FARM AUCTION PRICES (AVERAGE)</p>
<p>Grain  Week to Aug 2  previous week  month/month  yr/yr change</p>
<p> Wheat    57.66 zl/q     57.28 zl/q    11.0 pct     -14.1 pct</p>
<p> Rye	42.02 zl/q     41.79 zl/q     6.0 pct	-1.8 pct</p>
<p> Barley   50.71 zl/q     50.09 zl/q     9.2 pct     -10.6 pct</p>
<p>NOTE: zl/q = zlotys per quintal.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom+48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
